---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import '../styles/home.css';
---

<Base title="nomicon" section="home">
  <main class="home">
    <section class="intro">
      <h1>Things you can poke at</h1>
      <p>
        Interactive explainers for game programmers: engine fundamentals, a real ECS running in your browser, game AI, physics, networking, and labs for
        pathfinding, tactical analysis and game feel. Every example runs live, so change it and see what happens.
      </p>
    </section>
    <div class="cards">
      <a class="card" href="/engine/">
        <span class="kicker">Foundations</span>
        <h2>engine</h2>
        <p>
          What the hardware and the engine underneath actually do: cache lines and data layout, handles and allocators, fixed
          timesteps, determinism, spatial partitioning from grids to octrees, job systems, threads and fibers, profiling, and hot reloading code. The "why" under
          the flecs lessons.
        </p>
        <span class="go">Start here →</span>
      </a>
      <a class="card" href="/flecs/">
        <span class="kicker">Lessons</span>
        <h2>flecs</h2>
        <p>
          The flecs entity component system, explained with a live world in every lesson. Add components and watch archetypes form, see
          which tables a query matches and what it caches, step systems, and fire observers.
        </p>
        <span class="go">Start the lessons →</span>
      </a>
      <a class="card" href="/ai/">
        <span class="kicker">Lessons</span>
        <h2>game ai</h2>
        <p>
          How game agents choose what to do, move and read the map: utility scoring, behaviour trees, goal-oriented and HTN planning,
          steering and context steering, avoidance from separation to ORCA, formations and terrain analysis, all live so you can
          watch them think.
        </p>
        <span class="go">Start the lessons →</span>
      </a>
      <a class="card" href="/physics/">
        <span class="kicker">Lessons</span>
        <h2>physics</h2>
        <p>
          How rigid-body engines work, on a small 2D engine you can pause and step: broadphase, contact manifolds, solvers that hold
          stacks, sleep, fast bodies, joints and characters. Then real Jolt, Box3D and Bullet side by side in your browser, Chaos and PhysX,
          and wiring physics into flecs through handles.
        </p>
        <span class="go">Start the lessons →</span>
      </a>
      <a class="card" href="/network/">
        <span class="kicker">Lessons</span>
        <h2>networking</h2>
        <p>
          How networked games hide the network, on one small game over a simulated connection you can make worse: latency, jitter
          and loss, snapshots and interpolation, prediction and reconciliation, lag compensation, lockstep and rollback.
        </p>
        <span class="go">Start the lessons →</span>
      </a>
      <a class="card" href="/pathing-lab/">
        <span class="kicker">Lab</span>
        <h2>pathing lab</h2>
        <p>
          Paint a map and watch A*, HPA*, navmeshes, roadmaps and vehicle planners search it, step by step, side by side. With concept
          notes for each idea.
        </p>
        <span class="go">Open the lab →</span>
      </a>
      <a class="card" href="/tactics-lab/">
        <span class="kicker">Lab</span>
        <h2>tactics lab</h2>
        <p>
          Terrain analysis for AI on a 2.5D map: clearance, choke points for movement and for sight, openness, cover generation by
          scanning and by sampling, exposure to threats, and picking the best cover. With concept notes for each idea.
        </p>
        <span class="go">Open the lab →</span>
      </a>
      <a class="card" href="/feel-lab/">
        <span class="kicker">Lab</span>
        <h2>feel lab</h2>
        <p>
          A platformer with every game-feel setting exposed: acceleration, jump height and timing, fall gravity, coyote time, jump
          buffering, corner correction, input delay, camera smoothing and juice. Turn one off and feel what breaks.
        </p>
        <span class="go">Open the lab →</span>
      </a>
    </div>
  </main>
</Base>
